420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-15T13:40:36-08:00","id":313264,"title":"","content":"Let's go ahead and be a hero here: spending 2 glamour to activate Stone 3: Display grandiose might. I assume the catch does not apply - as this would be a practical purpose (down to 2 glamour!)<br /> Ath+Wyrd: <a href=\"http://invisiblecastle.com/roller/view/4718606/\" target=\"_blank\">http://invisiblecastle.com/roller/view/4718606/</a> success!, so Freddy gets +2 (wyrd) to strength for lifting, jumping, strong man type stuff<br /> <br /> Now let's move some cars: str+sta+2 = 8<br /> Stabilize (-2): <a href=\"http://invisiblecastle.com/roller/view/4718611/\" target=\"_blank\">http://invisiblecastle.com/roller/view/4718611/</a> EXCEPTIONAL<br /> and drag to safety (-4): <a href=\"http://invisiblecastle.com/roller/view/4718614/\" target=\"_blank\">http://invisiblecastle.com/roller/view/4718614/</a> uh oh...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2734,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2734-atwannabe","user":"ATwannabe","date":". 11-15-2014, 04:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2734-atwannabe","name":"ATwannabe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2734_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-15T21:31:13-08:00","id":313484,"title":"","content":"If I can pull this mook from the jaws of death without a Strength roll, I'll do it, and leave him there. If it requires any kind of athleticism, I''ll need to jumpstart him with s'more Spring magic and let him save himself.<br /> <br /> Here's a roll for the latter, because things don't go smooth. <br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://invisiblecastle.com/roller/view/4719016/\" target=\"_blank\">Jumpstarting an idiot, 1 glamour, 1 WP (8d10.hitsopen(8,9)=3)</a><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3994-dwyad","name":"Dwyad","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-15T23:01:36-08:00","id":313532,"title":"","content":"Note, I would like to confirm that I am unable to login at invisible castle, have no been told that my id is already taken and have never received a confirmation email to activate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3961-thrythlind","name":"Thrythlind","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-16T19:58:34-08:00","id":314158,"title":"","content":"OK, I'm gonna see if it'll let me create accounts for you guys to use. Hang tight!<br /> <br /> Dwy, the roll to pull him out of the car is Dex + Strength. May as well give it a shot, right? Don't forget your seeming blessing!<br /> <br /> Carp, are you taking a look at the files immediately or waiting 'til later? <br /> <br /> Thryth, give me a quick Int + Resolve roll, please - if I haven't gotten to you with an account, just make sure to note Free's name.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-16T21:01:27-08:00","id":314184,"title":"","content":"Alright, let's give this a swing... <a href=\"http://invisiblecastle.com/roller/view/4720407/\" target=\"_blank\">Dex+Strength, pull that mook out! (4d10.hitsopen(8,9)=1)</a><br /> <br /> Made it!<br /> <br /> As to the account registration clusterfuck? It's honestly a non-issue. Roll under your character's name, any rolls that aren't under that name don't count. Done an' done.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3994,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3994-dwyad","user":"Dwyad","date":". 11-17-2014, 12:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3994-dwyad","name":"Dwyad","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-17T02:41:58-08:00","id":314348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://invisiblecastle.com/roller/search/1522497/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://invisiblecastle.com/roller/search/1522497/\" target=\"_blank\"> Loading... </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://invisiblecastle.com/roller/search/1522497/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://invisiblecastle.com/roller/search/1522497/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Two 9s for two successes total. Character noted as &quot;Free - Thryth&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3961-thrythlind","name":"Thrythlind","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-17T14:28:44-08:00","id":314840,"title":"","content":"OK so &quot;removing a barrier&quot; falls under the catch of &quot;Ogre's rending grasp&quot; stone 2 - so Freddy is going to just go ape on this thing, and activate the contract - every little bit helps.<br /> <a href=\"http://invisiblecastle.com/roller/view/4721127/\" target=\"_blank\">http://invisiblecastle.com/roller/view/4721127/</a> success, so I guess the door loses 1 durability point, not sure if that will help the rending of the door from its hinges but I am hoping it will.<br /> <br /> as for the door - Str + Sta? extended? Let me know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2734-atwannabe","name":"ATwannabe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2734_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-17T14:31:00-08:00","id":314843,"title":"","content":"Also - I could use reminding on the extent to which our characters know each other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2734-atwannabe","name":"ATwannabe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2734_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-17T15:33:43-08:00","id":314857,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure if Mal particularly knows Fred. They probably know eachother's names and occupations, at least, because Lost can instantly recognize other Lost, and it's almost unthinkable they haven't met after passing by one-another. so many times.<br /> <br /> 'Course, if Fred's ever had need for a medic, they might know eachother a little closer. She's probably kinda famous for patching up Lost with hard-to-explain wounds. If he's a hedge-delver, in the Autumn tradition, he's probably had a few of those, and Goblin Fruit can only fix so much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3994-dwyad","name":"Dwyad","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-17T17:47:26-08:00","id":314966,"title":"","content":"Strength + Stamina, and the door has 2 Durability (reduced by one). I'll rule that to break the door open you only need to deal 3 damage (so 4 successes - two to bypass the durability plus two). Or you can do it over a couple of turns.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1168,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","user":"HobbitGuy1420","date":". 11-17-2014, 08:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-17T18:16:31-08:00","id":314979,"title":"","content":"What was the results of my roll?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3961-thrythlind","name":"Thrythlind","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-17T20:08:05-08:00","id":315031,"title":"","content":"Thryth, I PMed it to you. You should see it in your messages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-17T20:16:27-08:00","id":315034,"title":"","content":"Dale's looking at the files immediately. No time like the present after all.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-18T18:14:27-08:00","id":315797,"title":"","content":"OK. It'll take hours (or the application of time-dilating effects) to read through both sets of files thoroughly, but here's what you manage to get from a relatively quick scan. <br /> <br /> Mr. Voyczyk is the owner and CEO of a good-sized communication conglomerate. The missing property in question is a basalt gargoyle statue which was taken from Mr. Voyczyk's penthouse apartment half a week previously. None of the security measures in the home (which include alarms on all of the doors and windows and pressure sensors in the floor of the gallery in which the statue was housed) were set off, but there are also no obvious signs that anyone <i>circumvented</i> them, either - the first sign that something was wrong was when the security guy in the building stopped by the bank of monitors and saw the protective case empty. Apparently the video recordings of the room fuzz out with static for about 30 seconds, and when they come back, the case was empty. <br /> <br /> Voyczyk's head of security found no fingerprints and no obvious DNA or fibers. The statue itself weighed several thousand pounds and was encased in a high-tech protective plexiglass case. You notice that there's not a great deal of information on the statue's provenance. It appears to have been from the late medieval period, but there's no documentation of precisely *how* he got it - the obvious assumption is that there was something extralegal involved in its acquisition. <br /> <br /> The redhead disappearances are described in a forum post that can kindly be described as &quot;tinfoil hat chic.&quot; The author describes a number of boys just at driving age who disappeared anywhere from the day of their birthday to two months before they turned seventeen. All but one include full names - the second includes only a last name and a reference to a high school in the suburbs where the boy attended school before disappearing. There's enough here to start investigating, but there's not a whole lot to go on immediately. <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\">((Give me a quick wits + Investigation each to put together any immediate conclusions about the cases, -2 for the disappearances 'cuz there's not much data there yet. Let me know if you want to use any powers or if there are any circumstances you think should offer a modifier.))</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-18T20:01:04-08:00","id":315843,"title":"","content":"I meant to post yesterday but got caught up in editing the Numenera gameplay audio from my one-shot nights. <br /> <br /> 24 minutes down. Only 2:21 left to go. Then gameplay session 2. <br /> <br /> I feel I'll be on the sixth game before I'm finished posting Numenera.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3961-thrythlind","name":"Thrythlind","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-18T21:34:27-08:00","id":315905,"title":"","content":"Numenera, huh? How does that play? The setting looks fantastic, but I was curious about how it works story and gameplay wise","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-19T01:40:54-08:00","id":316060,"title":"","content":"If you are used to d20 and other heavily gamist and simulationist systems, it will seem like an amazing step forward (at least, when I find people who like it seems like they all have mostly experience with rules-systems that tend to have more minutiae like d20),<br /> <br /> If you come from HERO, Fate, WoD or a lot of other heavily narrative systems you will likely feel horribly lied to when told that the game was a narrative exploration based game.<br /> <br /> The first section of game play was rather annoying...we heavily modded for the second session of gameplay.<br /> <br /> We were also not impressed with the printed adventure, admittedly that could have been better embellished if I were doing a full campaign...since I'm just doing oneshots I don't want to put that effort in. Also, flaws in a published adventure are generally forgivable for a system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3961-thrythlind","name":"Thrythlind","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-19T02:36:33-08:00","id":316097,"title":"","content":"Mr. Voyczyk case: 3 successes - <a href=\"http://invisiblecastle.com/roller/view/4722867/\" target=\"_blank\">http://invisiblecastle.com/roller/view/4722867/</a><br /> <br /> Redhead case: 2 successes - <a href=\"http://invisiblecastle.com/roller/view/4722868/\" target=\"_blank\">http://invisiblecastle.com/roller/view/4722868/</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-19T17:13:05-08:00","id":316704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Strength + Stamina, and the door has 2 Durability (reduced by one). I'll rule that to break the door open you only need to deal 3 damage (so 4 successes - two to bypass the durability plus two). Or you can do it over a couple of turns. </div> </div> </div>Alright: Str 3 + Sta 3 + 2 (from contract earlier) let's see if 'Ol Freddy can't manage it in one. If not, he'll try again<br /> <a href=\"http://invisiblecastle.com/roller/view/4723475/\" target=\"_blank\">http://invisiblecastle.com/roller/view/4723475/</a> = 2 succ<br /> <a href=\"http://invisiblecastle.com/roller/view/4723477/\" target=\"_blank\">http://invisiblecastle.com/roller/view/4723477/</a> = 3 succ<br /> Reached the goal!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2734-atwannabe","name":"ATwannabe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2734_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-19T17:14:17-08:00","id":316706,"title":"","content":"As for knowing each other - that is pretty much what I thought. I have a feeling that Freddy would have definitely called on the services of a back-alley surgeon, so I'm sure they know each other's names.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2734-atwannabe","name":"ATwannabe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2734_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-19T17:37:31-08:00","id":316726,"title":"","content":"Actually, that's only 1 sux toward it - the durability negates the first 2 successes of every roll. You still need at least one 3+ roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1168,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","user":"HobbitGuy1420","date":". 11-19-2014, 08:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.t